ArrayBytes":5308416,"riverCells":0,"lakeCells":0,"watershedCount":0,"generatedFeatureCount":0,"invalidFeatureCount":0}}},"packageManifest":{"packageType":"recipe","liveState":"excluded","privateWorldbook":"excluded","createdAt":"2026-10-19T19:01:42.000Z","generatorVersions":{"terrain":"terrain-v2","layers":{"topography":"topography-v2","hydrology":"hydrology-v2","climate":"climate-v2","ecology":"ecology-v2","atmosphere":"atmosphere-v1","physics":"physics-v1","authoredFeatures":"authored-features-v2","liveState":"live-state-v1","atlas":"atlas-v1"}},"assetVersions":{"builtin":"aetheria-natural-v1","external":[]},"attribution":{"author":"Aetheria","application":"Aetheria","applicationVersion":"1.1.5"},"privacy":{"containsConversationState":false,"containsPrivateWorldbook":false},"recipeFingerprint":"11de6a6f","readableBook":"Lantern Quay is a small harbour town on a cold, foggy coast, built up a cliff above its harbour. At the bottom is the Quay: the harbour wall with its three test lamps, the slipway, the fish market and the salvage shed on the strand. Halfway up the cliff path is the Tidewater Inn. At the top is the Works, the glassworks that grinds lenses for every lighthouse on the coast.\n\nOff the strand lies Gull Rock, a tidal island with the Works' test tower and an old keeper's cottage, reached by a stone causeway that floods at high water.\n\nInland the ground rises to a heather moor with a ring of standing stones called the Teeth, where jackdaws nest, and a flooded sand quarry. The road to Harrowgate crosses the moor.\n\nIt is cold and grey most of the year, fog in the mornings, the sea never far off."},"cover":"data:image/webp;base64,","checksum":{"algorithm":"crc32","value":"ba9ca420"}}